  "strategy": "Approach and rationale\nOur multi-resolution Bayesian optimization strategy focuses on iteratively refining solutions from lower to higher resolutions while escaping local optima. This addresses the non-convex search space by:\n\n1. Balancing exploitation and exploration through Bayesian optimization\n2. Maintaining dimension consistency across resolutions via constrained interpolation\n3. Implicitly handling the integral constraint through projection steps\n\nThe key bottleneck is the high dimensionality (up to 1000 features) and the expensive computation (O(n\u00b2) convolution) of the max-correlation objective.\n\nMathematical specification\n**Variables**:\nh \u2208 [0,1]^n (step function samples)\nConstraint: sum(h) = n/2 (maintained via projection)\n\n**Objective**:\nmin C5 = max_k \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx (scaled by dx=2/n)\n\n**Representation**:\n- Initial solution from `initial_h_values` (if available)\n- Design space as constrained [0,1] hypercube with integral constraint via projection\n- Use Gaussian Process surrogate to approximate objective function\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. **Parent Initialization**:\n   - Validate parent solution (if initial_h_values provided)\n   - Project to feasible set if needed\n   - Prepare Bayesian Optimization framework\n\n2. **Resolution Cycle**:\n   for resolution_step in [base_resolution, base_resolution*2, ..., max_resolution]:\n      if time_remaining() < \u03b5 break\n      new_resolution = next_resolution(scale_factor)\n      S = base population at old_resolution\n      X_train = interpolate X_old\u2192new_resolution(S)\n      y_train = evaluate_survival(X_train)\n\n   Adaptive sampling: \n\n   f(x) = C5(h)\n\n   Acquisition function: Expected Improvement (EI) with dropout noise model\n\n3. **Local Search** (within resolution):\n   function = EI(aquisition_function)\n   new_x = optimizer_minimizer(function, current_point)\n   \n   Optimization framework:\n   - Use BayesOpt library\n   - Tweak BO parameters based on improvement rate\n   - Maintain adaptive length of BO runs\n\n4. **Resolution Transfer**:\n   Low \u2192 High: Simultaneous coordinate scaling and re-normalization preserving integral\n   High \u2192 Low: Linear warping minimizing integral change\n\n5. **Termination Checks**:\n   Relative improvement < 1e-4 or timing out\n\nSearch choices and useful variations\n**Key settings**:\n- `base_resolution` = 100\n- `resolution_scale` = [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32]\n- `population_size` = 20\n- `BO_patience` = 10 (minimum iterations)\n\n**Adaptive components**:\n- Temperature-scheduled Simulated Annealing restarts\n- Dimensionality-adjusted mutation strength\n- Performance sharpening: If improvement stalls, reduce new-resolution scaling factor\n\nExplicit configurations:\n1. Initialization\n2. Optimization hyperparameters\n3. Transfer mechanics\n4. Selection thresholds\n\nCompute budget and robustness\n**Estimates**:\n- BO evaluation of one point: O(n log n)\n- Relative total time: L \u00d7 time_750 (base_case)\n- Memory: (n \u00d7 L) samples (L=logarithmic)\n\n**Wall-clock response**:\n- Budget checks at each GP update\n- Graceful timeout by returning best candidate\n- Projection counter: Limit \u22652 per point\n- Batch processing: 8 evaluations/second \u0394n=50%\n\n**Fallback**:\n- Memory manager handles dimension jumps\n- Batched-to-projection repair candidates\n- Requires BayesOpt framework (scikit-optimize)\n\nValidation and return contract\nReturn (h_values, best_c5, n_points) where:\n- np.all(0.0<=h_values), np.all(h_values<=1.0)\n- abs(sum(h_values) - n_points/2) < 1e-8\n- c5_returned < parent's 0.380866\n- Time-measure guards at each budget phase\n- Outline validation logic for h_values projection and integral consistency\n\nSpecific operations implemented:\ndef bayesian_optimize_at_resolution(n, timeout=None):\n    ... # returns best h for resolution n\n\ndef transfer_solution(old_h, new_n):\n    ... # ensures integral preservation\n\ndef evaluate_survival(h): # returns C5 via helper\n    ... # projects to feasible set if needed\n\nThe solver framework writes and resolves progress iteratively, dynamically adjusting objectives based on historical improvement metrics.",
